    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ebf070ed_b68ab1cf",
        "filename": "virtualizationservice/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 752,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-02T00:00:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These are types, not attributes, right? Can\u0027t it be attribute? Otherwise, we will be disallowing files attributed as system_file_type, but has a different concrete type (ex: system_lib_file)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 752,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 752,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "53cc5cac42f75422880d0a3315690a6b49cdd988",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cea4c2b8_d782b081",
        "filename": "virtualizationservice/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 752,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-02T08:39:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s mostly deliberate.\nI\u0027m open to adding more types if there\u0027s a need.\nAllowing attributes would be a lot more complicated, and also make the check less useful, since it\u0027s pretty easy to add attributes to an arbitrary type.",
      "parentUuid": "ebf070ed_b68ab1cf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 752,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 752,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "53cc5cac42f75422880d0a3315690a6b49cdd988",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
